    "updated_at": "2020-10-06T00:34:39Z",
    "body": "I experimented with the style @MartinSGill used and it seems like it would be helpful to reference the style of another module. A variable like $module.style can be necessary to transition between modules -> or even better a $prev/next.style variable to just get the adjacent module style. \r\n\r\nIf you don't you will end up with black spaces between them or worse, color mismatches. You can work around it by hardcoding the values, but then if you have a module that dynamically changes style like $battery/$username or if you change the order of the modules you have to redo your config again.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
