    "created_at": "2022-11-29T05:14:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-29T05:24:22Z",
    "body": "This has been around for quite some time so I would love to see it implemented. Since since then I have started to use rust I would be willing to give it a show although there seem to be others that already have implementations.\r\n\r\n> or even better a $prev/next.style variable to just get the adjacent module style.\r\n\r\nI think all that is needed is just a $prev.style variable since determining the next would mean that a second pass would be required to build the full prompt. I feel like that is the minimum necessary to implement this although having an automatic styling and just providing a character to style it to would be sick too.\r\n\r\nEdit: After a bit more digging it seems that when the format was added this exact problem was mentioned but not further discussed since the issue was closed for the 0.45.0 release. https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/624#issuecomment-612888024",
